ip type="definition">Any significant occurrence in the system or an application that requires a user to be notified or an entry to be added to a log.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="152534">event</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456845">پېښه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7960_262487_457221"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The speed at which the CD drive will record the data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262487">CD burner speed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="457221">سي ډي ثبتووني چټکتیا</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7971_121145_456618"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to technologies for converting textual (ASCII) information into synthetic speech output. Used in voice-processing applications requiring production of broad, unrelated, and unpredictable vocabularies, such as products in a catalog or names and addresses. This technology is appropriate when system design constraints prevent the more efficient use of speech concatenation alone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121145">text-to-speech</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456618">متن وینا ته</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7971_121145_457249"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to technologies for converting textual (ASCII) information into synthetic speech output. Used in voice-processing applications requiring production of broad, unrelated, and unpredictable vocabularies, such as products in a catalog or names and addresses. This technology is appropriate when system design constraints prevent the more efficient use of speech concatenation alone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121145">text-to-speech</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="457249">TTS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7971_262703_456618"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to technologies for converting textual (ASCII) information into synthetic speech output. Used in voice-processing applications requiring production of broad, unrelated, and unpredictable vocabularies, such as products in a catalog or names and addresses. This technology is appropriate when system design constraints prevent the more efficient use of speech concatenation alone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262703">TTS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456618">متن وینا ته</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7971_262703_457249"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to technologies for converting textual (ASCII) information into synthetic speech output. Used in voice-processing applications requiring production of broad, unrelated, and unpredictable vocabularies, such as products in a catalog or names and addresses. This technology is appropriate when system design constraints prevent the more efficient use of speech concatenation alone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="262703">TTS</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="457249">TTS</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7976_346946_457699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Capable of producing successful results.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="346946">effective</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="457699">اغېزمن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="803_44794_456119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The work area on a computer screen that simulates the top of an actual desk. The desktop contains the Recycle Bin and other icons (shortcuts to programs, files, folders, and various types of documents such as letters, reports, or pictures) that you can arrange on the electronic desktop just as you would arrange real objects on top of a desk.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="44794">desktop</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456119">سرپاڼه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8036_116444_456587"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A horizontal window at the bottom of a parent window in which an application can display various kinds of status information. The status bar can be divided into parts to display more than one type of information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="116444">status bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456587">انکړ پټه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8040_149410_456828"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A query that uses the UNION operator to combine the results of two or more select queries.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="149410">union query</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456828">یووالي پوښتن</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8058_125224_456637"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The _ character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="125224">underscore</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456637">لاندکرښکه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="8058_319169_456637"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The _ character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319169">LOW LINE</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="456637">لاندکرښکه</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="807_22891_455947"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of starting or resetting a computer or a device. When first turned on (cold boot) or reset (warm boot), the computer runs the software that loads and starts the computer's operating system, which prepares it for use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="22891">bootstrap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="455947">پيلون</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="807_22891_455948"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of starting or resetting a computer or a device. When first turned on (cold boot) or reset (warm boot), the computer runs the software that loads and starts the computer's operating system, which prepares it for use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="22891">bootstrap</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="455948">پیلون سېسټم</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="807_730299_455947"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of starting or resetting a computer or a device. When first turned on (cold boot) or reset (warm boot), the computer runs the software that loads and starts the computer's operating system, which prepares it for use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="730299">startup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="455947">پيلون</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="807_730299_455948"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of starting or resetting a computer or a device. When first turned on (cold boot) or reset (warm boot), the computer runs the software that loads and starts the computer's operating system, which prepares it for use.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="730299">startup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="455948">پیلون سېسټم</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="808_264640_457267"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A fraction that is written on a downward angle: the diagonal fraction bar is placed down and to the right of the numerator, and the denominator is slightly down and to the right of the fraction bar.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="264640">skewed fraction</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ps-AF"><ntig><termGrp><term id="457267">بییلی کسر</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">AFG</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="g